1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:05,210
Listen up, squirt! You're not on anybody's radar!

2
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:06,920
The only winner here is me!

3
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:08,880
Senpai...

4
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:09,630
Huh?

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,210
Basketball isn't some merciful sport
that you can just crawl back to...

6
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:15,080
...after you made the choice to drop out.

7
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:19,750
Shit, was he always this good?!

8
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,880
Nice pass, Koney!

9
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:30,960
Just watch me, you damn pipsqueak!

10
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:33,330
I'm DEFINITELY going to leave you in the dust!

11
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,960
Acceleration Mode....on!

12
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,250
Taro?!

13
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:40,000
Huh?!

14
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:43,830
That shot is off!

15
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,460
It's going to come down near you, Momoharu!

16
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,080
Rebound!

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:47,040
I know already!

18
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:52,920
We've been at this for more than
20 minutes straight now... so how?!

19
00:00:53,630 --> 00:00:55,380
All right, Kato! Gimme that ball!

20
00:00:57,670 --> 00:00:58,710
I'm out?

21
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,880
This is... a direct order from your coach.

22
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:07,830
Goddammit...

23
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,630
Goddammit!

24
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:11,040
I can keep going!

25
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,750
I know I can still run!

26
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,580
I'm the top scorer here.

27
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,790
Just try and stop me if you can!

28
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,130
They've switched over to full-court D!

29
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:32,080
Hey Nanao.

30
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:35,380
Let's make a substitution.

31
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:38,250
Taro! Behind you! It's a screen!

32
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,830
Weak sauce. That won't work on me!

33
00:01:44,290 --> 00:01:46,790
He just straight-up ignored my brilliant screen!

34
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:50,290
You're nothing but a crazy nutjob!

35
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,960
Huh?!

36
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:57,000
Goddamn! Could you have made that pass
any harder to catch?!

37
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,920
Go ask Chiaki to give you
some passing lessons, dumbass!

38
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:05,790
The pass went through!

39
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
This brat is nearly dead on his feet!

40
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
There's no way I'm letting him score one on us!

41
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:11,670
I will.

42
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:22,080
Rebound!

43
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:29,210
Ugh, that damn idiot!

44
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:30,830
Momoharu!

45
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:35,750
Show me one more time, what it looks like to fly!

46
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:41,580
Having a 9-point lead is total chump change!

47
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:43,250
We're gonna tie it right back up!

48
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,000
Whoa!

49
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:46,540
What a jump!

50
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,540
HELL YEAH!

51
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:50,500
I have a proposition.

52
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:53,380
Do you think you can commit
to being our point guard for a bit?

53
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,380
Huh?

54
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:00,290
I'm going... to score us some points.

55
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,040
Huh? Wait...

56
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:04,500
Are you up for it?

57
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,420
I'll do whatever it takes.

58
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:10,210
No matter what... I'm not letting us lose this game!

59
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:19,080
Kagami ni senaka mukete ayumu hodo ni toozakaru yume yo

60
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:23,580
Massugu kimi to mukiaitai

61
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:30,210
Dekinai jibun e to "never mind"

62
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,080
Ahiru no Sora

63
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:44,040
Nagare sagyou de waketeyuku yume

64
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:47,330
Muki? Fumuki? Iwaba rongai?

65
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:51,790
Koe mo naku kietetta koe

66
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,790
Tameiki sura denai

67
00:03:55,170 --> 00:04:00,960
Hito no sei ni shitatte owarenai

68
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:04,920
Me no mae ni kiritatta ima

69
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:08,960
"Koetai" to kokoro ga sakenderu

70
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:16,500
Dekinai wake o sagasu nara daredemo dekiru sa

71
00:04:16,710 --> 00:04:24,040
Agaki hashitta sono saki mada shiranai jibun to deau

72
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:30,420
Kabe ni kizamikonda rakugaki to "never mind"

73
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:34,540
Ima asu e to hazume

74
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,960
You want me... as point guard?

75
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:47,920
Last Play

76
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,130
Yeah.

77
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:48,880
I don't expect you to start doing it right away, though.

78
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:51,130
But, wait, then what's Chiaki going to do?

79
00:04:51,710 --> 00:04:54,040
Well, I've been thinking about the balance of our team,

80
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:53,380
Hey Kite!

81
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:54,040
Huh?

82
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:57,880
and I came to the conclusion that it's a waste
to have Chiaki as point guard with all his height.

83
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,210
Come on! Let's do some Dribbling Sumo!

84
00:04:56,210 --> 00:04:56,960
No way!

85
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,880
Sumo?

86
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:02,880
Given that our team is lacking players, it's important
to have the right person in the right position.

87
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:07,670
It's possible that Chiaki might be able
to go on the offensive instead.

88
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:11,960
Meanwhile, that means you can take control of the game,

89
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,080
and use your skills to dominate
from outside the three-point line.

90
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:18,750
I think that arrangement would make our team
a lot stronger than it is now!

91
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,080
Let's get back in the lead, one basket at a time!

92
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:27,710
Hm? #15 switched over to taking possession of the ball.

93
00:05:28,130 --> 00:05:29,580
Kurumatani...

94
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,000
Their #7 is heading for low-post!

95
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,380
Katori! Change your man!

96
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:34,790
Watch out above you!

97
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:40,290
I get it! Because Chiaki is so tall, we can net
some easy points if he's close to the basket!

98
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,830
The situation isn't as simple as you think.

99
00:05:44,710 --> 00:05:48,210
We're not going to be able to pass through their defense
as easily as we did before.

100
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:52,000
Good passing requires high precision
and height lends itself to that.

101
00:05:53,130 --> 00:05:58,380
Being able to play basketball and being able to play
as point guard are two totally different things.

102
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:01,250
Going off the cuff like this might end poorly.

103
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:05,540
On top of that, there's one thing
I never explained to Kurumatani.

104
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:09,750
When a player like him switches over
to being point guard, they lose something important.

105
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:11,170
And what's that?

106
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,380
The ability to be assertive.

107
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,920
Switch!

108
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:17,080
Don't leave him open!

109
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:19,380
Chiaki!

110
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,330
Dammit!

111
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:24,420
Crap! He got himself trapped!

112
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,460
Don't you think Tinytown could've just gone
for a three there instead?

113
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:30,880
There's a whole 24 seconds on the shot clock.

114
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:35,460
The common approach for everybody on offense
is to use that time to its fullest and not rush.

115
00:06:35,710 --> 00:06:36,670
Kite...

116
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:42,750
Missing a three in the first few seconds that results
in a turnover is absolutely something to avoid.

117
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:43,880
Plus...

118
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:49,330
The more focused you are on how to move the ball
around, the less inclined you are to try and score.

119
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,460
That's especially true for a shooter like him.

120
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:54,250
And now...

121
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:57,580
...he can't shoot three-pointers the same way anymore.

122
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:00,710
Bad pass!

123
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,290
You pushed it way too far inside!

124
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:06,830
Nabe! Get on #5! Don't let him run free!

125
00:07:10,670 --> 00:07:12,750
Crap! I screwed that up!

126
00:07:13,130 --> 00:07:14,750
Defensive foul on #8!

127
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,170
Sorry, guys.

128
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:16,920
Forget it.

129
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,250
Their fouls have started to pile up!

130
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:20,670
Just one more and they'll have five team fouls!

131
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:22,830
Don't cower away from them.

132
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:27,420
They'll steal chickenshit passes like that every time.

133
00:07:27,830 --> 00:07:29,460
You can't help being small...

134
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,420
...so make bold moves instead.

135
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:34,750
Right!

136
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:43,420
Ms. Yuka Kurumatani...?!

137
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:48,460
I take it you must be Madoka.

138
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:49,580
Uh, yes!

139
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:52,080
My mother had a lot to say about you.

140
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:54,830
Oh, that lady...

141
00:07:55,790 --> 00:07:59,830
I was surprised to learn you were
Ms. Yabuuchi's little sister. Such a small world!

142
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:02,250
I wouldn't have agreed to come here otherwise!

143
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:05,960
I hear that you've been doing a lot
for my little Sora. Thank you.

144
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,290
Not at all.

145
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:10,670
Wow... she's really beautiful!

146
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,670
That's the sound of Sora running.

147
00:08:15,670 --> 00:08:18,460
You can tell?! That's amazing!

148
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:21,460
There's a distinctive tempo in how he slides.

149
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,330
He's got a number of quirks like that.

150
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:26,250
I guess he hasn't developed much as an athlete yet.

151
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:30,540
Um, how about we go take a look inside?

152
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:32,460
There's not much time left in the fourth quarte-

153
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:35,290
No. I'm content with staying here.

154
00:08:35,290 --> 00:08:37,420
Huh? Um, but...

155
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:40,380
I just wanted to feel the excitement of the game in the air.

156
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:42,920
I didn't come here intending to do anything more.

157
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:47,000
Ms. Yabuuchi, I think that my 10 minutes are up.
Are we okay on time?

158
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,960
Your 10 minutes were up
before we even left the hospital!

159
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,710
But, um, maybe you could just...

160
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:54,960
...take a quick look from afar?

161
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:55,920
Madoka.

162
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:59,290
I'm afraid we can't take the time.

163
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,830
Since we snuck out of the hospital without permission.

164
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:09,790
Um, then...

165
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:13,080
Is there anything that you would like me to do?

166
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:14,290
Perhaps deliver a message?

167
00:09:15,170 --> 00:09:18,630
Oh! I could send you some pictures of him
during practice from my phone!

168
00:09:18,630 --> 00:09:21,710
I appreciate the thought, but that's not necessary.

169
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:23,130
But...

170
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:34,880
Actually... there is one thing that you could do for me.

171
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:39,830
Will you... make sure that Sora gets this?

172
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:42,000
A handmade charm...

173
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,960
Are you sure that's all you want me to do?

174
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:49,540
Yes. Oh, but please don't tell Sora
that this bracelet came from me.

175
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:50,670
Huh?

176
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:53,330
Would you be willing to just let him think
it's a gift from you?

177
00:09:53,630 --> 00:09:58,080
I mean, as far as Sora knows, I'm still in the dark
about him coming to school here.

178
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:02,080
After that, he took the entrance exams
for schools out here.

179
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:04,710
And eventually came stumbling into my house.

180
00:10:05,170 --> 00:10:07,710
His dad thought this would be the best thing for him.

181
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:10,790
Even though his mom told him not to come here?

182
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:11,790
Yeah.

183
00:10:11,790 --> 00:10:14,040
He's keeping it all a big secret from her.

184
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:17,670
So that he can go visit her the instant
he wins that tournament.

185
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,210
Um, okay, but I really don't think
he'll accept a gift from me...

186
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:24,830
Don't worry, you're totally Sora's type.
I'm sure he'd be overjoyed!

187
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:29,040
Um, no way, I'm sure you're just exaggerating.

188
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:31,000
So you won't do it?

189
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,210
Uh, well, I think I can handle it.

190
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:36,250
Thank you.

191
00:10:41,790 --> 00:10:44,130
Well then, please take good care of it.

192
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:45,130
Yes, of course.

193
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:47,040
I'll make sure that Sora gets it!

194
00:10:48,830 --> 00:10:52,420
I'm so sorry for making you put up
with my selfishness, Ms. Yabuuchi.

195
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:54,830
Uh-huh, sure. It's fine, just forget about it.

196
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:57,130
See you later then, Madoka.

197
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:58,630
Oh, sure.

198
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,210
Tell me something, Madoka.

199
00:11:04,210 --> 00:11:05,170
Yes?

200
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,170
Is my son...

201
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,630
...having a good time playing basketball?

202
00:11:16,830 --> 00:11:17,710
Yes.

203
00:11:24,710 --> 00:11:26,170
A steal!

204
00:11:26,630 --> 00:11:27,750
He cut Taro off!

205
00:11:27,750 --> 00:11:28,580
Unbelievable!

206
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:31,250
This brat... I thought he had run out of steam!

207
00:11:32,290 --> 00:11:35,000
Switch back to defense! Don't let them into the center!

208
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:37,170
My body feels so light.

209
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,920
I thought I was too tapped out to run anymore.

210
00:11:42,710 --> 00:11:45,580
But now I feel like... I have the wind at my back!

211
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,710
Look at that! He's totally free!

212
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,670
I see. This must be what having peace of mind is like.

213
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:59,500
I can feel Chiaki behind me...
he's encouraging me to fight on!

214
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:00,830
A two-handed shot?!

215
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:03,500
It's a three-pointer!

216
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:05,290
It's going to miss!

217
00:12:05,290 --> 00:12:06,460
It'll bounce off!

218
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:16,540
An alley-oop?!

219
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,750
He intended for it to be a pass from the get-go.

220
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,710
Amazing! I've never seen one in person!

221
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:28,040
Your timing was a little off.

222
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:29,920
Right!

223
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,290
Only three minutes left.

224
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,130
We WILL turn this around.

225
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:48,920
There was a foul!

226
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,130
Oh crap!

227
00:12:52,420 --> 00:12:54,580
Defensive foul! The basket counts!

228
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:57,380
All right!

229
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:56,750
Sick move.

230
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:57,380
Thanks!

231
00:12:58,130 --> 00:12:59,380
No way...

232
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:02,330
That's the third basket #7 has made
since going on the offensive!

233
00:13:02,330 --> 00:13:07,250
Kuzuryu            Kitasumiyoshi

234
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:07,080
Yeah, and we haven't gotten any rebounds
since their #4 started to pull himself together.

235
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:13,080
But wait, if their #7 could score like this, then why did
he wait so long to actually shoot any baskets?!

236
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:16,500
The answer is simple,
it's because he wasn't capable of doing so.

237
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:17,750
Huh?

238
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:23,920
His passes and leadership are quite impressive,
but unfortunately, he's not fast on his feet.

239
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:27,670
I assume it's too difficult for him
to drive to the basket alone.

240
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:30,170
And of course, he probably can't shoot long-range.

241
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:36,630
Katori realized this early on and adjusted his defense
to assure #7 didn't make it into the paint.

242
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:38,750
For real?

243
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Oh crap! I can't believe I screwed that up!

244
00:13:45,670 --> 00:13:46,460
Rebound!

245
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:49,330
Damn, he stole the prime position!

246
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,750
Here we go!

247
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:54,960
Holy cow!

248
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:58,380
I threw my entire body weight at him
and he didn't even budge!

249
00:13:58,670 --> 00:14:01,040
I can't believe he's powerful enough to do that!

250
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:04,580
Tachibana, get under the basket!

251
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,040
Don't let him shoot freely!

252
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:11,250
A pass?!

253
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:15,670
Somebody get on #15! Taro,
what the hell are you doing?!

254
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:17,540
I let my guard down!

255
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:21,250
Their #7 wasn't even looking this way
when he passed! How the hell?!

256
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:22,790
Shit!

257
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,210
And right in front of Nao, that bastard!

258
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:28,790
It's a three!

259
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:30,330
Go in!

260
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:35,790
It... it went in...

261
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,250
Hell yeah!

262
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:39,960
Kuzuryu            Kitasumiyoshi

263
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,920
Only a 4-point difference!

264
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:41,880
We've nearly turned this around!

265
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,500
Th-this is insane...

266
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:46,580
I can't believe they caught up with us
in such a short amount of time!

267
00:14:46,830 --> 00:14:50,000
That kid should be well beyond the peak
of his fatigue by now!

268
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,960
What is he made out of?!

269
00:14:57,750 --> 00:14:59,170
Out of bounds!

270
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:01,170
Throw-in with Kitasumi in possession!

271
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:02,830
Oh man, Nabe! That was so close!

272
00:15:04,710 --> 00:15:07,210
Player substitution for Kuzuryu High!

273
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:09,710
Hey, Nanao.

274
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,580
Where did you learn to do athletic taping like this?

275
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:15,710
Uh, why do you ask?
You know how my family runs a sports shop.

276
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:17,670
We have a lot of customers who are professional trainers,

277
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,250
so I learned some from them
and then I studied the rest myself.

278
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:24,290
I'm sorry. Did I put it on too tight or something?

279
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,210
No. Thank you, you saved my ass.

280
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:29,880
Now I can keep running without holding myself back.

281
00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:41,790
Defense! Defense! Defense!

282
00:15:32,250 --> 00:15:34,210
There's hardly any time left in the game!

283
00:15:34,210 --> 00:15:36,290
Do whatever you can to keep them from scoring!

284
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:39,830
Shore up under the basket!
And don't let #7 get free no matter what!

285
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,290
I'm so stupid!

286
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,790
Did I forget what I came here to do?!

287
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:48,580
Did I forget what drove me to join this team?!

288
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:52,790
I did it... to make sure these guys win, dammit!

289
00:15:54,630 --> 00:15:55,500
It got knocked away!

290
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,080
Loose ball!

291
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,210
Whatever you do, don't let go!

292
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,210
Yasu!

293
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:03,830
Listen, shitheads... you'll have to kill me
before I let this ball go!

294
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,580
Held ball!

295
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:08,670
Throw-in with Kuzu High in possession!

296
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:10,830
All right!

297
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,750
Nice work, Yasuhara.

298
00:16:14,710 --> 00:16:17,290
That whistle freaked me out, I thought I'd fouled again.

299
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:22,210
We gotta make this possession count.

300
00:16:22,210 --> 00:16:24,460
If we can't score,
then kiss our chances of winning goodbye!

301
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:27,960
Hey, Yasuhara, if you get the ball,
then feel free to go for the shot.

302
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,960
Right!

303
00:16:30,210 --> 00:16:33,170
Guys... we're gonna win this. No matter what!

304
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:37,040
That ball is going in the basket!
Watch out for fouls, guys!

305
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:37,710
Okay!

306
00:16:37,710 --> 00:16:44,130
Shoot it in! Let's win! Shoot it in! Let's win!

307
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:44,130
Do your best out there... Sora!

308
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:55,170
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

309
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,960
Shoot it in! Let's win! Shoot it in! Let's win!

310
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:54,330
Here they come! Keep them out of the paint!

311
00:16:54,330 --> 00:16:55,170
Right!

312
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:57,630
Shoot it in! Let's win!

313
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,000
That low?!

314
00:17:03,210 --> 00:17:05,380
Konishi! They're coming from both sides!

315
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:07,040
Don't let them get into position!

316
00:17:09,330 --> 00:17:12,210
You're not getting anything past me!
I'm holding you off right here!

317
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:13,880
Konishi!

318
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,080
Through the legs?!

319
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:22,670
Sweet!
Yeah!

320
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,920
Damn, I'm good.

321
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,460
No dude, that was all me.

322
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:26,790
It was MY pass that did it!

323
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:30,380
Kuzuryu            Kitasumiyoshi

324
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,080
Only a 2-point lead now?!

325
00:17:28,290 --> 00:17:30,080
No way... after all we did...!

326
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:32,710
What the hell are you blockheads doing?!

327
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:36,080
Listen here! Don't you dare let this game
go down to the wire!

328
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,540
Shut your face, stupid geezer!

329
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:40,750
We don't need you to tell us the obvious!

330
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,750
C'mon, Kuzu High! Fight!

331
00:17:44,290 --> 00:17:46,250
The next basket is mine, no matter what it takes!

332
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,790
Like hell I'm letting that pipsqueak show me up again!

333
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,420
Kato! Pass it here!

334
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:57,130
Damn! They went for an easy pass over my head!

335
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,500
Don't panic, Sora!

336
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:00,880
Just let up your guard on him!

337
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:03,170
He's telling me to pull back and defend the inside!

338
00:18:04,670 --> 00:18:06,250
Don't let anybody get past you!

339
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:08,540
This is it! We have to keep them from scoring!

340
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:11,290
Hey, is that the right call? Aren't we short on time?

341
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:13,080
Shouldn't they be going after the ball?

342
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,290
No, this is good.

343
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:18,130
If we want to win, we have to stop their shot
and then go sink our own.

344
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,290
We absolutely cannot afford anything else.

345
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:22,830
There's 30 seconds left with a 2-point difference.

346
00:18:23,290 --> 00:18:26,580
This is a really tough situation, even for Kitasumi.

347
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:30,210
They should do whatever it takes
to assure they score on this possession.

348
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:32,540
They won't risk a shot from long-range!

349
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:36,880
If we have our defense focused on keeping them
out of the paint, our chance will come eventually.

350
00:18:39,830 --> 00:18:41,000
A three-pointer?!

351
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:45,830
Miss! Miss, dammit! Miss!

352
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,080
It hit the rim!

353
00:18:48,250 --> 00:18:49,290
Rebound!

354
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:50,750
Dammit!

355
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:52,000
It came up short!

356
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,380
That prick, he didn't even hesitate!

357
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,000
Momoharu! Screen them out!

358
00:18:57,830 --> 00:18:59,670
Shit! He beat me to it!

359
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:02,710
I fucked up!

360
00:19:05,330 --> 00:19:06,420
Yes!

361
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,000
We got the offensive rebound!

362
00:19:08,170 --> 00:19:10,580
Konishi pass it back out! We need to regroup!

363
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:11,460
This is bad.

364
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,040
We're finished if they keep hold of the ball.

365
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,330
Huh? But why?

366
00:19:14,330 --> 00:19:16,130
What about the 24-second violation?

367
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:21,630
The shot clock gets reset to 14 seconds
after a rebound on a shot that hits the rim.

368
00:19:22,830 --> 00:19:23,920
Seriously?!

369
00:19:25,750 --> 00:19:26,790
Yasu!

370
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,670
I'm done... my legs just can't keep going anymore...

371
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,080
I hadn't considered this.

372
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:36,500
They're going for an even bigger lead,
no matter how risky!

373
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:38,130
I got this!

374
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:43,960
Shit, he's better than I thought...

375
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,080
Go in!

376
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:49,580
Go in!

377
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:51,170
Miss!

378
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:53,750
It fell!

379
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:55,210
Get the rebound!

380
00:19:55,630 --> 00:19:58,000
Please! We really need this!

381
00:19:58,420 --> 00:20:00,330
Come on!

382
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:06,250
Shit! I couldn't get a hold!

383
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,080
You're such a waste of space!

384
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:11,830
It's headed out of bounds!

385
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:16,460
I'm not giving up!

386
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:19,580
I can't help but wonder why I'm sticking with this team.

387
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,040
Oh, there he is.

388
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:23,920
Yo, Kite! Teach me some more about how to dribble!

389
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,750
Not everybody plays the game
just to support somebody else.

390
00:20:26,750 --> 00:20:28,250
Hey! You bums!

391
00:20:28,250 --> 00:20:30,330
Get ready to train your asses off!

392
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:32,630
We may not be able to actually score any points, but...

393
00:20:32,630 --> 00:20:35,330
...we'll do all the other stuff that only we can accomplish!

394
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:38,040
It would be great if you guys went to the inter-high.

395
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,710
I want to know what it feels like
to share the joy of victory with a team.

396
00:20:42,830 --> 00:20:46,130
Until the very last second... none of us are giving up!

397
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:04,250
THIS ONE IS MINE!

398
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:06,170
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

399
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:07,630
Nice dive, bro!

400
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:08,960
Defend the basket!

401
00:21:09,170 --> 00:21:09,920
Everybody go back!

402
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:11,330
Chiaki!

403
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,000
He kept it in!

404
00:21:14,170 --> 00:21:15,210
Live ball!

405
00:21:24,290 --> 00:21:25,750
Kite is totally open.

406
00:21:25,750 --> 00:21:27,330
We can score 2 points for sure.

407
00:21:27,330 --> 00:21:28,380
Do I pass?

408
00:21:29,630 --> 00:21:30,580
No.

409
00:21:31,170 --> 00:21:33,040
Our whole team is already running on empty!

410
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:36,040
If this goes into overtime, then we'll lose for sure!

411
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,460
The only way to win this...

412
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:41,170
...is by going all in... from here!

413
00:21:44,830 --> 00:21:46,000
I couldn't reach it!

414
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:49,040
Son of a bitch!

415
00:21:51,330 --> 00:21:52,540
A three!

416
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:00,380
GO IN!

417
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:17,960
Hitori ja umaku ikanaku temo

418
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:22,170
Kikkake nante tanjun sa

419
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:29,130
Mienai deguchi ni hikaru ga sashite

420
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:33,290
Asu wa soko ni arunda

421
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:40,000
Hitori nanka ja nakatta

422
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:45,210
Kono me ni utsuru keshiki no naka ni

423
00:22:45,210 --> 00:22:51,540
Kimi ga ireba doko made datte ikeru sa

424
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:56,420
Kitto genkai nante nainda

425
00:22:56,420 --> 00:23:01,580
Kimi to ireba tsuyoku narunda

426
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:08,670
Nando demo tachiagatte susunde ikou

427
00:23:08,790 --> 00:23:16,710
Oh oh oh, oh oh oh, oh oh oh,

428
00:23:16,710 --> 00:23:19,670
Saigo no ichibyou made

429
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:22,500
Akiramenaide busukatte

430
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:29,580
Kono michi no saki wa kanarazu kagayaiteru kara

431
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Tears

432
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:34,250
Next episode: "Tears."

